# Ubiquitous language

## Rule

- Use consistent project domain terms in prompts, plans, code symbols, comments, tests, and documentation.
- Do not introduce synonym drift for established core concepts.

## Required behavior

- Reuse existing repository terminology when names already exist.
- If a new domain concept is introduced, define it once and reuse the same name thereafter.
- When ambiguity exists between near-synonyms, ask which term is canonical before broad edits.

## Naming constraints

- Prefer names that match repository vocabulary over generic placeholders.
- Keep type/function/class naming aligned with existing feature language.
- In tests, express behavior with the same domain terms used in production code.

## Documentation alignment

- When adding or changing a key domain concept, update relevant process docs/examples so terminology remains coherent.
